+## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)
+
+[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime
+directories and manages dedicated `tmux -S` servers with no ambient or
+default-server discovery or reuse (pinned Sections 4.2, 4.C-4.E).
+`EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf relative to a pinned root
+handle (`mkdirat`, never a path-string `MkdirAll`) and enforces three
+independent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID
+ownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is
+verified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one
+server socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit
+override, whether it arrives as a `TMUX` environment value, an inherited
+socket, a default path, or the conventional `default` name. `Acquire`
+reaches the server through the caller-appropriate path: foreground
+attaches to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S`
+server whose stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while
+background contacts only the already-running authenticated broker and
+its attested server, and otherwise returns the typed
+`capability_unavailable` refusal with realm/readiness details — there is
+no fallback to direct creation, and every background test arms a spy
+spawner that fails the run if it is ever invoked. `CheckLiveAttestation`
+admits only a complete live observation (passed sentinel and
+provider-auth smoke bound to the exact server generation, provider
+build, and macOS version); the `launchctl managername` hint and any
+cached sentinel observation travel for diagnostics only and authorize
+nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs through
+injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux process
+anywhere.
+
+Run the focused tests and coverage with:
+
+```bash
+go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1
+go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1
+```
+
+Run the narrowing battery (29 narrowing mutants, one supplementary
+additive row, plus one harmless control) with:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py
+```
+
+The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer
+through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and
+reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`
+additionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one
+raw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are
+attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`. The package adds no `ax` command, no
+`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test
+matrix with its stated bounds lives in
+[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).
