+// Package tmuxserver owns AX private tmux server management: owner-only
+// runtime directories and dedicated tmux -S servers with no ambient or
+// default-server discovery or reuse. It is the first leaf of the
+// production-tmux-backend story.
+//
+// Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 4.2 (tmux backend, dedicated -S
+// server, credential-sensitive creation, background broker-or-refuse,
+// launchctl managername as diagnostic hint only, cached observations
+// never authorize resume), Section 4.C (operation vocabulary cited for
+// the wrapper entrypoint shape only), Section 4.D (capability evidence
+// cited landed), and Section 4.E (sensitive runtime state is owner-only
+// and non-replicable).
+//
+// Division of authority (composed, never forked): the caller vocabulary
+// (foreground/background) comes from internal/axpane, which already
+// gates the wrapper decision over it; the capability_unavailable typed
+// refusal comes from internal/axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable, which
+// enforces the exact Section 15.3 detail set; path grammars come from
+// internal/scalar (absolute root, relative member, UUIDv7 session);
+// lexical containment comes from internal/secprim.Guard; the ambient
+// environment-name rule comes from internal/secprim.IsEnvName; argv
+// shape validation comes from internal/secprim.CheckArgv. What this
+// package owns is the composition no landed package provides: the
+// descriptor-relative runtime-directory commit (mkdirat from a pinned
+// root handle, not a path-string MkdirAll), the three independent
+// custody gates (mode, ownership, containment), the four-vector ambient
+// non-use proof (environment variable, inherited socket, default path,
+// conventional name), the background broker-or-refuse acquisition path
+// with its no-fallback gate, the live-attestation authorization gate
+// over which cached sentinel and managername observations carry no
+// authority, and the dedicated -S argv builder.
+//
+// Bounds: no ax CLI surface, no lifecycle operations (create, attach,
+// status, quiesce, stop, terminate, restore belong to the sibling
+// leaves), no ConPTY process control, no provider process, no mesh
+// transport, and no evidence signature verification (caller-supplied
+// probes report attestation; this package decides over their reports).
+// Windows ownership is verified through the platform ACL where the OS
+// exposes it and is otherwise a stated bound pinned by a tripwire test.
+// No test in this package starts a tmux process: every broker, server,
+// and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies, and the
+// suite passes with no tmux installed.
+package tmuxserver
